#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""dipstick -- how much is left on your AI coding subscriptions, and which one is main.

Reads the quota your Claude Code / Codex / Antigravity subscriptions have left,
says when each one recovers, and remembers which one you picked as main so your
launch command can ask for it. It reports and remembers; it never launches
anything or decides for you.

Nothing here sends a prompt to a model. A probe turn would open a fresh
rate-limit window -- the opposite of what a gauge should do -- so every source is
a passive read or a metering endpoint that costs no quota.
  Codex   payload.rate_limits inside session rollout files (cached by inode)
  Claude  GET /api/oauth/usage, the endpoint the CLI itself uses. Reads the OAuth
          token from the login keychain, so the first run raises a macOS prompt.
  agy     RetrieveUserQuotaSummary on a running agy's local language server
  live    CODEX_HOME of running codex processes

Usage
  dipstick                    text report
  dipstick --json             machine-readable snapshot (menu bar app reads this)
  dipstick --html [PATH]      write a self-contained page, no server needed
  dipstick --serve [PORT]     local web UI, click to set main (127.0.0.1:8787)
  dipstick --set-main KEY     one of the keys printed by --json, or "auto"
  dipstick --main-cmd         print the launch prefix for the current main
  dipstick --lang ko|en       display language (the web UI has a switch too)

Config (all optional) -- ~/.config/dipstick/config.json
  {"reserve": {"Claude": 20},          # keep this % for the subscription's own use
   "policy":  {"Codex ProLite": ["1st", "default lane"]},
   "imminent_minutes": 60}
"""
